package agentsdoc

import "strings"

// writeV04dHostSection documents what 0.4d adds for the host's side:
// `append` (the store, a Batch, the fd 3 message, the `batch` entry, and
// play's step), `ready.messages`, and `--screen`. It names no path of the
// repository, since the project briefing (ProjectMarkdown) is this same text.
func writeV04dHostSection(b *strings.Builder) {
	b.WriteString("### v0.4d: append and the host\n\n")
	b.WriteString("- `Append(path, v)` (Go) adds to the value at `path` in place, so a host streams a reply without sending the old value back: a string takes a string (`v` must be one), and an array takes `v`, any JSON value, as **one** element at its end (an array `v` is one element, never spread). It is a `Set` of the new value in every other way: a redraw, and the derived values recomputed. Any other case is an error that changes nothing: `append \"P\": \"P\" is missing`; `append \"P\": \"P\" holds TYPE, not a string or an array` for `null`, a number, a boolean, or an object; `append \"P\": \"P\" holds a string, and the value is TYPE, not a string`; `append \"\": the root is not a string or an array`; `append \"P\": \"P\" is a reserved path` for `@focus`, `@screen`, and `@theme`. A derived path or a malformed path gives the error `Set` gives, unchanged. `TYPE` is `a number`, `a boolean`, `an object`, `an array`, or `null`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `(*Batch).Append(path, v)` queues an append and checks its arguments as `b.Set` does; the value at the path is checked when the batch is applied, against the store as the earlier writes of the batch left it (`b.Set(\"log\", []any{})` then `b.Append(\"log\", x)` gives `[x]`), and a failure there applies nothing. Over `tuimark host`, the fd 3 message `{\"type\": \"append\", \"path\": P, \"value\": V, \"id\": N}` is acked as a `set` is, and a `batch` entry may hold `\"op\": \"set\"` (the default) or `\"op\": \"append\"`; any other `op` makes the message malformed and nothing of it is applied.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `play` takes the step `append:PATH=JSON` (`{\"append\": {\"path\": P, \"value\": V}}` in a `--script`, exactly those two members): `Append(PATH, value)` on the document's data. It cannot hold a space, as `set:` cannot; a step that fails is a usage error with the reason above, `tuimark: play: step N (append:PATH=JSON): append \"PATH\": …`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `ready` of `tuimark host` gains `messages` after `diagnostics`: the fd 3 types the child accepts, `[\"set\", \"bind\", \"batch\", \"get\", \"reply\", \"append\", \"commit\"]`. `protocol` stays `1`: a parent checks `messages` before it sends a type an older child would report as unknown, and a child whose `ready` has no `messages` accepts exactly the first five and reads only `path` and `value` of a `batch` entry. A `commit` message (`lines`, or `template` with optional `with` and `props`) is accepted and checked, and answered `commit: not in inline mode` unless the session is inline (`tuimark host FILE --inline`, which a document that writes `version` refuses with `tuimark: host: inline mode needs a <tui> without version`, exit 1, nothing on fd 4). A commit is acked once its rows are written, is printed at once while an event waits for its reply, and one sent before a `reply` with `quit` is printed before the leave sequence.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `tuimark run FILE --screen ID` and `tuimark host FILE --screen ID` start the session on that screen: `Set(\"@screen\", ID)` is applied once the document is loaded and `--data` bound, before the first frame (a parent's own `set` of `@screen` lands after it). An id no screen has is `tuimark: run: no screen with id \"ID\"` (`tuimark: host: …` under `host`, with nothing on fd 4) and exit 1, before the terminal is touched. A reload under `run` keeps the screen the session is on.\n\n")
}
